  "body": "**Stacked on #957** (issue #852, branch `issue/852-necked-tool-envelope`). The base here is upstream `main`, so until #957 merges this diff also shows #957's commit (`54ed3fe7`); this PR's own change is the single commit on top (`fix(sim): drill reach, cross drill and probe stylus read the body's band stack`). Merge #957 first.\n\n## What changed\n\n#835 moved most of the stack laws onto a modelled tool body's band stack (`Cutter::body`) but left three on the cylinder enclosing the body. #957 later did the same for the neck. This PR moves those last three onto the bands, so they judge the same shape the simulation draws:\n\n- **Axial holder-face law** (`operation::drill_reach::axial_reach`): each band's face disc (`bottom + band.above`, at that band's own radius) is checked against the material top over that disc (prior grid read at that radius). A refusal names the offending band: \"tool T's body band (dia. D, A mm above the tip) sinks to Z ...\".\n- **Cross-drill holder law** (`drill_reach::cross_holder`): the per-move law (the on-station tube, or the swing's swept rectangle) runs once per band, at that band's face, radius and length. The per-band body is split out into `band_clear`. `seg_dist`, `holder_approach` and `hull_dist` moved verbatim into `drill_hull.rs` to keep the file under 400 lines.\n- **Cross-drill part law** (`operation::cross_part::part_clear`): now takes the body-carrying cutter (`Cutter::of(tool).with_body(..)`, the one `generate` builds) and re-judges it against the tool's geometry (`Cutter::judged`).\n- **Probe stylus** (`operation::probe_op::stylus_cutter(tool, stack)`): rebuilt as ball, stem, probe body (the record's shank band), then the body's own bands, checked as a `BodyBands` of the stylus stack.\n- `run_job_arms` now builds `geom` / `holder` / `cutter` once at the top, so the probe and drill arms can use them. The code at the old site moved up unchanged.\n- The enclosure wording (\"judged here by the cylinder enclosing it\") is gone wherever the bands are read. It stays only for the fallback case: a body whose stack does not fit the record (`body_judged::falls_back`, used for generator refusals), or one that does not fit the stylus (the probe note).\n\nSafety: no body, or a stack equal to the holder cylinder, carries nothing. The laws then read exactly the `holder()` cylinder they read before, with the same refusal text (pinned to the byte). A carried band that is non-finite, starts below the shank's top, or is wider than the enclosing holder is not trusted, and the cylinder stands in. No holder modelled still sweeps nothing, and a non-finite holder field is still refused by name. The probe is handed a stack only when the tool has a body.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/842-band-stack-drill-probe.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nEach law is pinned three ways: a stepped body whose flange clears is no longer refused, a flange that reaches is still refused, and a tool with no body reads unchanged.\n\n- Axial (`crates/app/src/operation/drill_reach_body_tests.rs`): `a_stepped_body_whose_flange_clears_the_wall_is_not_refused_by_the_axial_holder_law`, `a_stepped_body_whose_flange_sinks_beside_the_wall_is_still_refused_by_the_axial_holder_law`, `a_tool_with_no_body_reads_the_holder_cylinder_bit_identically`\n- Cross holder (same file): `a_stepped_body_whose_flange_clears_the_ear_is_not_refused_by_the_cross_holder_law`, `a_stepped_body_whose_flange_meets_the_ear_is_still_refused_by_the_cross_holder_law`\n- Cross part (`crates/app/src/operation/cross_part_tests.rs`): `a_stepped_body_whose_flange_clears_the_part_is_not_refused_by_the_cross_part_law`, `a_stepped_body_whose_flange_meets_the_part_is_still_refused_by_the_cross_part_law`, `a_tool_with_no_body_reads_the_cutter_it_always_did`\n- Probe and end to end (`crates/app/tests/tool_body_drill_probe.rs`): `a_stepped_body_over_the_stylus_is_judged_by_its_bands`, `a_flange_over_the_stylus_that_meets_the_part_is_still_refused`, `a_probe_with_no_body_reads_its_one_band_unchanged`, `a_drawn_stepped_body_on_a_drill_is_judged_by_its_bands_not_the_enclosing_cylinder` (through `operation::generate` with `SetToolBody::spun`), `a_drawn_body_on_a_probe_is_judged_by_its_bands_end_to_end`\n\n## Readings\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, full plan, final head): green - tools, sim, motion, app (incl. lib, tool_body_drill_probe, drill_reach*, drilling_cross*, probe_*, tool_body*), ui: 5 steps, 0 failed, 1526 tests passed, 22.2 min wall\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Moved goldens: none. No golden or snapshot carries a tool body. No snapshot PNG touched.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- An imported-mesh body (#368) end to end on a cross drill. The cross laws are pinned at law level with hand-built band stacks; the drawn-profile path is pinned end to end for the axial drill and the probe.\n- The multi-axis shank-avoidance dodge (`motion::multiaxis::avoid`) stays on the cylinder: it is a generator choice, not a verdict, and #835 lists it as kept.\n- Lathe cross drilling with a body: same code path as the mill-turn cross drill. Its existing suites ran in the quick gate.\n\nChangelog: Drill reach, the cross-drill holder and part laws, and the touch probe's stylus reach judge a modelled tool body by its band stack, so a stepped body is no longer refused for a flange that never reaches the material (#842)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0.\n\nFixes #842\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
